From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rick Yiu <rickyiu@google.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jan 2024 17:26:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: moto-holi: Change UCLAMP_BUCKETS_COUNT to 20

Using the default setting 5 means the first bucket contains the
uclamp values from 0 to 19 (in percentage), in this case, if the
uclamp.min setting of a group is under 20, it will fall into this
bucket with other groups that have uclamp.min set to 0, which
increase the possibility of over boost. By setting the bucket
count to 20 will ease this situation, while a uclamp.min greater
than 4 will fall into a different bucket.

Bug: 170487162
Change-Id: Ife96b199bee36faedc8e129ade17e475cdbe44e0
Signed-off-by: Sevenrock <sevenrock@hotmail.de>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lineage_moto-holi.config | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lineage_moto-holi.config b/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lineage_moto-holi.config
index 2fb842f1e32a..ba9a0b45f83a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lineage_moto-holi.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lineage_moto-holi.config
@@ -95,3 +95,4 @@ CONFIG_WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT_DEFAULT=y
 CONFIG_QCOM_KGSL_IDLE_TIMEOUT=58
 # CONFIG_PROCESS_RECLAIM is not set
 CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED=y
+CONFIG_UCLAMP_BUCKETS_COUNT=20
-- 
2.39.5

